msgid "r0_bell_keeper_dialog"
msgstr "Quarry-stone bells with iron tongues warned three valleys until the slide. Nobody has operated the chain since, whatever sounds at night."

msgid "r0_gardener_dialog"
msgstr "Squabbit take dry seed; Elofly only settle here when the ridge wind drops."

msgid "r0_pass_surveyor_dialog"
msgstr "The old warning stones carried across valleys. West wind and quarry runoff arrive with the new tone; weather may be playing abandoned work."

msgid "r0_quarry_prospector_dialog"
msgstr "Wet cracked stone and a buried iron strap answer one another here. That can sound without anybody ringing a bell."

msgid "r0_south_shepherd_dialog"
msgstr "The lower night tone follows Split Crown's west face when fog presses low. Grandmother's quarry warnings kept that rhythm, but sounded brighter."

msgid "world_synthesis_campaign"
msgstr "The Ashenbell Highlands"
